# Input
```astro
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<script>alert("inline")</script>
<script type="module">console.log("module")</script>
<script nonce={nonce}>console.log("nonce")</script>
<script define:vars={{ value }}>console.log(value)</script>
<script type="text/plain">data</script>
<script type={scriptType}>data</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.astro:2:1 lint/nursery/noAstroUnsafeInlineScripts ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i Avoid inline scripts without a src attribute.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <script>alert("inline")</script>
      │ ^^^^^^^^
    3 │ <script type="module">console.log("module")</script>
    4 │ <script nonce={nonce}>console.log("nonce")</script>
  
  i An inline script is harder to restrict with a Content Security Policy and cannot be managed as a separate script resource.
  
  i Move the script to a separate file and reference it with a src attribute, or configure a narrowly scoped allowance.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

